fun-cosyvoice3-0.5b-2512-demo
=============================

This repository contains an on-device port (C++ inference library, Python business layer, web UI) of
Fun-CosyVoice3-0.5B-2512 for Qualcomm NPUs.

Upstream model and code
-----------------------
Fun-CosyVoice3-0.5B-2512 (FunAudioLLM)
  model: https://huggingface.co/FunAudioLLM/Fun-CosyVoice3-0.5B-2512 (rev 29e01c4)
         https://www.modelscope.cn/models/FunAudioLLM/Fun-CosyVoice3-0.5B-2512
  code:  https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice (rev 074ca6d)
  License: Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE)
The model files themselves (quantized QNN context binaries and host-side tensors derived from the upstream weights) are
not distributed in this repository. The voice cloning models (speech_tokenizer_v3.onnx, campplus.onnx) are downloaded
from the official release by the user (docs/VOICE_CLONING.md#1-prepare-the-environment-and-model-resources).

Third-party components
----------------------
demo/assets/clone_assets.npz
  Constant tables of the upstream frontend's feature extractors (mel filterbanks and windows), computed with
  openai-whisper (MIT), torchaudio (BSD-2-Clause) and librosa (ISC) by the voice preparation process.

nlohmann/json (compiled into libcosyvoice3.so)
  Copyright (c) 2013-2025 Niels Lohmann <https://nlohmann.me>
  License: MIT (see sdk/lib/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt)

pocketfft from NumPy (compiled into libcosyvoice3.so)
  Copyright (C) 2004-2018 Max-Planck-Society, Martin Reinecke; Copyright (c) 2005-2023, NumPy Developers
  License: BSD-3-Clause (see sdk/lib/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt)

text_tokenizer (compiled into libcosyvoice3.so)
  Our C API (Apache License 2.0) over the Hugging Face tokenizers crate 0.20.4 (Apache License 2.0) and its
  dependencies (MIT / Apache License 2.0), with the Oniguruma regex library (Copyright (c) 2002-2021 K.Kosako,
  BSD-2-Clause). Every crate and its license text: sdk/lib/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt

OpenSSL 3.0.2 (libcrypto, statically linked into libcosyvoice3.so)
  Copyright The OpenSSL Project Authors
  License: Apache-2.0 (see LICENSES/OpenSSL.txt)

ICU, OpenFST and MeCab are compiled into the native library. See sdk/lib/LICENSES/native-text/.
WeText-derived frontend code retains Apache 2.0 terms (see sdk/third_party/wetext/).

SDK Python dependencies include NumPy and UniDic. The Demo also uses Flask, Werkzeug,
  SoundFile and huggingface_hub. See sdk/lib/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

Inference runtime
-------------------------
The bundled Pandora Runtime wheel and its SDK integration use Apache License 2.0.
See the wheel's LICENSE and NOTICE.
The SDK bundles Qualcomm QNN under the terms in sdk/lib/qnn248/. Aidlux LMS and the device drivers are system dependencies.
They are not part of this repository and are covered by their own licenses.

Voices
------
The three prepared built-in voices under sdk/assets/voices/ derive from these recordings:
  female-zh  AISHELL-1 (https://www.openslr.org/33/), BAC009S0736W0134, Apache License 2.0
  female-en  LibriSpeech test-clean (https://www.openslr.org/12/), 121-121726-0003 (2.48-6.58 s), CC BY 4.0
  male-en    LibriSpeech test-clean, 2300-131720-0036 (0.40-4.40 s), CC BY 4.0
LibriSpeech attribution: V. Panayotov, G. Chen, D. Povey, S. Khudanpur,
"LibriSpeech: an ASR corpus based on public domain audio books", ICASSP 2015.
The conditioning values are preserved by the flat-package migration. Recordings,
optional previews and derived voice conditions retain their source permissions.
Personal user voices are not included or automatically published.
